# The environment, rebuilt by setup.sh on whatever machine this lands on
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Working files and outputs. Nobody else's footage belongs in this repo.
work/
out/
raw/
models/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.MOV
*.wav
# Transcripts of real footage live in work/ and are ignored by the rule above. These
# two trees hold hand written test fixtures that kit_check.py needs, and a blanket
# *.srt rule quietly kept all nine of them out of the first public push, which is why
# five of the self tests reported SKIP on a fresh clone.
*.srt
!fixtures/**/*.srt
!specs/*.srt

# Internal research carrying account ids, not part of the product
HOSTING-AND-PACKAGING.md

.DS_Store

# Scraped research output. Regenerate it with yt_probe.py; it is not ours to ship,
# and this directory has already had to be purged from this history once.
research/

# A measured niche profile belongs to whoever paid for the measurement.
# Useful locally, and no part of what a stranger clones.
specs/niche-aoyl.json

# Session material and anything written ABOUT the owner rather than for a buyer.
#
# This folder is one push from public and has no private mirror to fall back on, so
# a file like this landing here is a disclosure rather than a mess. It has happened
# three times, the last one a write-up quoting the owner under their own name. The
# three files moved out on 2026-11-05 were moved outside this tree entirely.
#
# WHAT BELONGS IN THE BRAIN REPO INSTEAD: anything addressed to another session,
# any findings or measurement write-up that quotes the owner, and anything naming
# their machine's paths or their accounts.
#
# This stops the next one being ADDED. It cannot untrack one that is already in,
# and `git add -f` walks straight past it, so the publishing gates are still the
# thing that has to be run before anything goes up.
HANDOVER-*.md
REPLY-TO-*.md
findings/
